  "content": {
    "title": "Kentucky vs Santa Clara score: Otega Oweh shot saves Wildcats in March Madness",
    "text": "Updated March 20, 2026, 5:13 p.m. ETEditor's note: Keep up with all of Friday's action in USA TODAY Sports' live blog for all 16 first-round games today here.Just like Day 1, Day 2 of the Men's NCAA Tournament got started with a bang.No. 7 seed Kentucky survived an upset bid from 10-seed Santa Clara, escaping with a 89-84 overtime win. Otega Oweh hit a game-tying 3-pointer at the buzzer to send the game to overtime with the Wildcats trailing by three.Oweh also hit a pair of free throws to give Kentucky the lead for good in overtime.Oweh finished with a career-high 35 points, with 22 coming in the second half. He also added eight rebounds and seven assists. Mouhamed Dioubate added 17 points, eight rebounds and three blocks, while Brandon Garrison had 10 points and six blocks.Elijah Mahi led the Broncos with 20 points. Allen Graves added 17 points, including the go-ahead 3-pointer that was erased by the 3-pointer from Oweh. The game featured 20 lead changes and 12 ties.Stream Kentucky vs Santa Clara live with Fubo (free trial)USA TODAY brought you live updates from the 2026 NCAA Tournament first-round matchup between Kentucky and Santa Clara. Catch up here. Santa Clara vs Kentucky scoreTEAMS1H2HOTFSanta Clara31421184Kentucky29441689 Santa Clara vs Kentucky highlights Santa Clara-Kentucky final score: Wildcats 89, Broncos 84 Kentucky-Santa Clara final statsStatSanta ClaraKentuckyScore8489Field goals30-of-73 (41%)32-of-63 (51%)3-pointers12-of-33 (36%)10-of-28 (36%)Free throws12-of-13 (92%)15-of-21 (71%)Rebounds3840Assists1719Steals85Turnovers711Points off turnovers1710Blocks211Fouls2017Largest lead47 Kentucky survives Santa Clara upset bidKentucky survives a potential upset from Santa Clara with an 89-84 overtime win. Otega Oweh scored 35 points, including the go-ahead free throws in overtime and the game-tying shot to send the game to overtime. Otega Oweh puts Kentucky aheadOtega Oweh continues to cook in the second half after knocking down two free throws to give Kentucky a lead. Brandon Garrison's dunk pushes the lead to 83-79 with 48 seconds left. Otega Oweh ties game on a buzzer-beaterOtega Oweh hits a game-tying 3-pointer from near halfcourt to tie the game at 73-73 to send it to overtime. Allen Graves had hit a 3-pointer to give Santa Clara the 3-point lead after Kentucky tied it out of the timeout. Kentucky will have chance to tie, winKentucky will have the ball with 24 seconds left and a chance to win or tie the game. Allen Graves missed two free throws with a chance to ice the game potentially. Allen Graves gives Santa Clara lead with less than 2 minutes remainingAllen Graves hits a layup to give Santa Clara a 70-68 lead with 1:25 left. Kentucky calls a timeout. Kentucky leads Santa Clara by 3 at final media timeoutKentucky holds a 67-64 lead with 3:41 left in the game at the final media timeout. Santa Clara will shoot a pair of free throws after the media timeout with a chance to cut the lead to one.Otega Oweh has scored 16 of his game-high 23 points in the second half to help the Wildcats pull ahead, for the moment. He will need to be the closer for Kentucky today. Santa Clara opens up 4-point lead at media timeoutSanta Clara holds a 59-55 lead over Kentucky with 7:47 remaining in the game at the under-8 media timeout. The Broncos are getting hot from the field, hitting 6 of the last 7 shots and shooting 61% in the second half.Kentucky pushed its lead to a game-high seven points at 51-44 with 8:54 left in the half, but the Broncos have outscored the Wildcats 15-4 since to take their largest lead of the game. Kentucky leads by two in second halfKentucky holds a 46-44 lead with 13:21 at the first stoppage of the second half. The Wildcats are 3-for-5 shooting from 3-point range in the second half after struggling in the first half. Otega Oweh leads the way with 16 points, while Denzel Aberdeen has 11.Elijah Mahi leads Santa Clara with 12 points. Second half underway between Santa Clara-KentuckyThe second half between Santa Clara and Kentucky is underway. The Broncos hold a 31-29 lead over the Wildcats through 20 minutes. Santa Clara-Kentucky halftime statsStatSanta ClaraKentuckyScore3129Field goals11-of-31 (35%)12-of-29 (41%)3-pointers4-of-15 (27%)4-of-15 (27%)Free throws5-of-6 (83%)1-of-3 (33%)Rebounds2019Assists67Steals63Turnovers47Points off turnovers72Blocks13Fouls69Largest lead26 Santa Clara leads Kentucky at halftimeSanta Clara finishes the first half with just two leads; however, one of them comes at the intermission, as the Broncos lead Kentucky 31-29. Santa Clara led for just over 2 minutes in the first half.Elijah Mahi leads the Broncos with 10 points, while Denzel Aberdeen leads the Wildcats with eight.Kentucky had four turnovers in the last 5:30 of the first half and was in a 2:29 scoring drought. Kentucky, Santa Clara struggling from 3-point rangeKentucky still holds a slim 20-18 lead at the third media timeout of the first half with 7:26 left. The Wildcats hit their first two 3-pointers, but both teams are struggling from deep since. They have shot a combined 4-of-19. Kentucky continues to lead Santa Clara in tight gameKentucky holds a 14-13 lead at the under-12 media timeout with 11:35 left in the half. The Broncos took their first lead at 11-10 out of the first media timeout on a 3-pointer for Christian Hammond, but the Wildcats scored back-to-back baskets to reclaim the lead.Otega Oweh still leads all scorers with five points for Kentucky, Jake Ensminger leads Santa Clara with four. Kentucky leading Santa Clara earlyKentucky holds a 10-8 lead over Santa Clara at the first media timeout with 15:10 left in the first half. The Wildcats jumped out to an 8-2 lead, but the Broncos evened the score with a 6-0 run.Otega Oweh's five points leads all scorers early on. Santa Clara vs Kentucky underwaySanta Clara and Kentucky are underway in the first round of the NCAA Tournament Midwest Region. The Wildcats have jumped out to a quick 5-0 lead. Pregame Starting lineups for Santa Clara-DukeSanta Clara:G: Brenton KnapperG: Christian HammondG: Jake EnsmingerF: Elijah MahiC: Bukky OboyeKentucky:G: Otega OwehG: Denzel AberdeenG: Collin ChandlerF: Andrija Jelavic⁠C: Malachi MorenoWhat time is Santa Clara vs Kentucky First Round game?Date: Friday, March 20Time: 12:15 p.m. ETLocation: Enterprise Center (St. Louis, Missouri)No. 7 Kentucky and No. 10 Santa Clara tip off at 12:15 p.m. ET on Friday, March 20, from Enterprise Center (St. Louis).What channel is Santa Clara vs Kentucky First Round game?TV: CBSNo. 7 Kentucky vs. No. 10 Santa Clara is airing live on CBS, with Spero Dedes, Jim Spanarkel and Jon Rothstein on the call.Watch the NCAA Tournament all March long with FuboHow to stream Siena vs Duke First Round gameStreaming: Fubo (free trial)No. 7 Kentucky vs. No. 10 Santa Clara is available to stream on Fubo, which offers a free trial to potential subscribers.Men's March Madness schedule todayHere's the schedule for all of Friday's NCAA Tournament action.All times Eastern12:15 p.m.: No. 7 Kentucky vs. No. 10 Santa Clara, CBS (Fubo)12:40 p.m.: No. 5 Texas Tech vs. No. 12 Akron, truTV (Sling TV)1:35 p.m.: No. 1 Arizona vs. No. 16 LIU, TNT (Sling TV)1:50 p.m.: No. 3 Virginia vs. No. 14 Wright State, TBS (Sling TV)2:50 p.m.: No. 2 Iowa State vs. No. 15 Tennessee State, CBS (Fubo)3:15 p.m.: No. 4 Alabama vs. No. 13 Hofstra, truTV (Sling TV)4:10 p.m.: No. 8 Villanova vs. No. 9 Utah State, TNT (Sling TV)4:25 p.m.: No. 6 Tennessee vs. No. 11 Miami (Ohio), TBS (Sling TV)6:50 p.m.: No. 8 Clemson vs. No. 9 Iowa, TNT (Sling TV)7:10 p.m.: No 5 St. John's vs. No. 12 Northern Iowa, CBS (Fubo)7:25 p.m.: No. 7 UCLA vs. No. 10 Central Florida, TBS (Sling TV)7:35 p.m.: No. 2 Purdue vs. No. 15 Queens, truTV (Sling TV)9:25 p.m.: No. 1 Florida vs. No. 16 Prairie View A&M, TNT (Sling TV)9:45 p.m.: No. 4 Kansas vs. No. 13 Cal Baptist, CBS (Fubo)10 p.m.: No. 2 UConn vs. No. 15 Furman, TBS (Sling TV)10:10 p.m.: No. 7 Miami vs. No. 10 Missouri, truTV (Sling 